# Round abplan: V4.1-Flash's prompt on two cards against the A6000 alone. --place bp, plan (b′): the A6000 runs
# every layer and the head as under plan (a), and the 3090 is an expert tier holding each layer's next ids after the
# stage's prefix, with the DSpark draft's reserve beside it when the draft is on
# (crates/placement/src/placement/workstation.rs:338-349). It runs against --place a, the A6000 alone with the 3090
# idle (workstation.rs:185-190), pp512 on the prose corpus, one two-card lease, same binary. The serving defaults
# hold otherwise: the residency unset is mid-p40-s1 under both placements (crates/levers/src/registry.rs:415-416);
# host streaming unset is on under a residency (registry.rs:508-510); no draft.
# The default on this machine is one card. The ds41 seat's --place is A
# (crates/gpu-gates/src/bin/shared/serve_seats/ds41.rs:215), and depth-ds41.sh's BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE defaults to a
# (tools/ref/depth-ds41.sh:662). No code default picks two cards. The best single-card placement is a: gate, the
# 3090 alone (workstation.rs:465), is the smaller card at its 250 W cap. Plan (b), the layer split at CUT 20
# (workstation.rs:193), is no --place word (a, gate, bp: crates/gpu-gates/src/generate.rs:113-115) and is not
# priced here.
# This card replaces the first draft of 10-05 (a GLM round, never sat). That draft read the window-apart pairs'
# off arms as the landed default, but unset streaming is on. It also put decode in a union band with the prompt,
# which no ab card can carry, because decode has no sign on paper (below).
#
# Resource timeline per token at decode, plan a after prose 512 [derived]. The basis is stgv41-ab.card's split of the
# measured 23.09 ms step (43.30 tok/s, rig-log 09-30#callstream-pp-a, on arm, the README row):
#   A6000 SMs  D 11.22 ms: the serial chain's fronts, joins and head; plus the shadow, 4.2..5.5 ms under the host leg.
#   Host CPU   H 11.87 ms: the routed slots past the card's, a layer at a time.
#   3090       idle.
#   PCIe       the go and join words and the residency's swaps, async.
#   The wall is Σ layers (front + max(H_l, shadow_l) + join) = D + H.
# At bp:
#   - The tier takes ~11 % of the host's routed mass (1,392 tier experts, 34.8 of 384 a layer, v41bp-ab.card:9-10):
#     H -0.9..-1.5 ms (a share of 0.08..0.13).
#   - The 3090's service of those slots, ~1..2 ms a step, runs under the reduced host leg.
#   - c_two, the two-card fixed cost, adds 0.5..2.5 ms. Its source is open, and docs/plan-triage.md carries
#     +1.9..+2.5 ms. The window-apart pair at the defaults (rig-log 09-30, the on arms: 44.28 against 43.30 tok/s,
#     -0.51 ms a step) fits c_two ≈ 0.8 ms beside a -1.31 ms tier term.
# Decode Δ = -1.0..+1.6 ms on the 23.09 ms step (tok/s -6.5..+4.5 %): no sign on paper. The decode question is
# v41bp-ab.card's (noninf, margin 2.0 %, 6 rounds), and this card reads it beside without deciding on it
# (`ratio prose d=512 prose/prose@place=a`).
# At depth 6 the lcg prompt of 6 ids is under STREAM_MIN_P, so there is no call stream. The residency climbs from its
# seed over the 96 steps, as the off arms' does: H ≈ 14..17 ms (the off arm's 27.74 ms step under a, rig-log 09-30
# #callstream-pp-a), and the tier's share of the lcg walk's skewed routing is 0.05..0.2: the tier saves 0.7..3.4 ms,
# c_two adds 0.5..2.5. Δ = -2.9..+1.8 ms, no sign either; read beside (`ratio d=6 ours/ours@place=a`).
# The prompt, this card's term. P 512 is one batch over 40 routed layers. The wall is a sum over the layers of the
# card route + max(host union + exchange, card shadow, tier service) + the join (tools/flow/ds41_prefill.py's
# docstring; body/prefill.rs Body::enqueue_group_chain).
#   - a's batch: 512 / 191.97 = 2,667 ms (README, on arm).
#   - The host union is 0.60..0.80 of that, 1,600..2,134 ms. [derived: callstream-pp-a's union of 9,746 ms is 0.86 of
#     the off P 4096 call's 11,282 ms; a 512 batch's card route is a larger share of its wall.]
#   - The tier serves its ids' slots and experts, 9..13 % of the union's: -144..-277 ms.
#   - The tier's serial cost on the host path costs 0.9..2.1 ms a layer-batch: the serve thread's enqueue before its
#     union and the join's mapped read, glmbp-pp.card's figure on the same machinery. Over 40 layers that is
#     +36..+84 ms.
#   - Its service on the 3090 is 1.3..1.5 ms a layer-batch: 34.8 experts x 16.8 MB at 650..800 GB/s, x in 8.4 MB,
#     the rows back ~5..7 MB at 26 GB/s. That is under the 40..53 ms union: shadowed, worth 0.
#   - PCIe: ~15 MB a layer-batch on the 3090's link and the join's ~5 MB of mapped reads on the A6000's. Host DRAM:
#     the tier's DMA, the same ~15 MB. NVMe: the engram rows, the same in both arms.
#   - The lever is the union's share; nothing here changes the flow.
#   - Net -60..-241 ms; the effect s / (W - s) is +2.3..+9.9 %. The window-apart pairs read +7.0 % (on arms, 205.48
#     against 191.97) and +6.1 % (off), inside.
#
# Sitting. Either its own invocation (a round is 2 loads, a and bp, of 2 arms each, prose:512 and 6; the load key is
# the binary, --place and the variables, depth-ds41.sh:838-850, so the two arms of a placement share one), from the
# tree that holds this card:
#   BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090 BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE=bp
#   BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/twocard-v41-ab.card' just depth-gpu-ds41 prose:512 6 prose:512@place=a 6@place=a
#   > <log> 2>&1
# or, at no box minutes of its own, read from v41bp-ab.card's sitting (its prose:512 rows carry the pp row), after
#   PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/ref/card.py check docs/cards/twocard-v41-ab.card --rounds 6.
# Wall [derived] of its own invocation: 4 rounds x 2 loads + the rotate warm-up, 9 processes at 1.6..2.2 min. The
# basis is the 09-29 windows: callstream-pp-a/-bp ran 5 processes of two arms in 12 / 11 min, less the P 4096 arm's
# ~13 s, plus the 6 arm's ~3 s, less the ~20 s of upload since (rig-log 09-30#v41-load-upload). Total 14..20 min.
kind: ab
question: does V4.1 prefill a 512-id prose prompt faster with the 3090 as its expert tier (--place bp) than on the
  A6000 alone (--place a), by the host union the tier takes less the tier's serial costs, at the serving defaults?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512 (each prose:512 row's `time prompt` record: the first 512 ids of corpus-prose.ids, one
  batch), A6000+3090 (the 3090 at its 250 W cap, idle under a), --place bp against --place a, residency and host
  streaming unset, no draft, same generate_ds41, paired by round: `ratio pp prose p=512 prose/prose@place=a`, less 1
unit: %
predict: 2..10
rounds: 4
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, V4.1's per-round pp ratios (glmbp-pp.card and callstream-pp-bp.card
  carry it), taken over the 0.6 % decode ruler for a 2.7 s prompt window
condition: one binary, every arm in one lease (BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090), a fresh process per placement and
  round, the order rotated every round; each bp row's load record names the A6000 then the 3090 and each a row's the
  A6000 alone (the runner fails any other); every row's residency column names mid-p40-s1, and each prose:512 arm's
  echoed lines carry a `call stream end` record (streaming on; the runner keeps `call` lines, depth-ds41.sh:486);
  each pp row reads n=512 and one batch; no Xid in any witness block, the 3090 at its 250 W cap in each; no row
  carries [cpu-busy], [other-busy] or [cold]; the full output to a file first
decide-in: cite pp512's two-card term in the 0.2.1 note with its conditions; the decode lines beside it carry no
  claim. Write the paired row to rig-log's A6000+3090 table, in place of the window-apart pairing's ratio. Sit
  v41bp-ab.card after 0.2.1 for the default flip.
decide-below: under +2 % the tier's serial cost on the prompt path runs past 2.1 ms a layer-batch, or its service
  leaves the union's shadow. The 0.2.1 note then claims no two-card prompt gain. Before any tier lever, run one
  functional bp prompt under BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 and read `stat prefill lb`'s union_ms against the tier's go and
  join.
decide-above: past +10 % the tier takes more than its id share of the prompt's host mass (the prose batch's hot
  experts in its id range), or streaming under a leaves less host mass than priced. Re-derive the share from the
  same stats window before the public row; v41bp-ab's decode band moves with it.
